  "verified_pin_count": 49,
  "formalized": [
    "Concrete association list has distinct row and hole keys; overwrite update preserves validity on a free destination, agrees exactly with the logical matching update and stores at most one pair per row.",
    "Direct row and owner lookup instrumentation agrees with the executable scans and makes at most r key comparisons on well-formed states.",
    "Table replay, guarded augmentation and outer matching loop agree exactly with the original matcher; typed matcher remains sound and never inconclusive.",
    "Retained support is computed once. One Boolean guard vector is used by matching, final certificate checks and witness masking. Explicit adjacency and guard-clause arrays are prepared once.",
    "The final explicit solver is exactly equal to the original for every input; supported checks, rejection behavior, SAT assignments and UNSAT results are preserved.",
    "Instrumented retained solver agrees with original run and counts actual clause-predicate evaluations. It makes at most (support cardinality+1) times clause count such evaluations, at most (b+1)*b for b=length(PEqualNP.Search.encodeCNF retainedFormula)."
  ],
  "partial_cost_limits": [
    "Lookup comparison counts exclude bit lengths and allocation.",
    "Retained clause-evaluation count excludes literal evaluation, negative-literal search, support/set operations, arithmetic and input/output encoding.",
    "The prior raw search event bound also omits work. No combination here establishes total bit runtime."
  ],
